nw-fermi-sb480 (0.6.5.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Anchor every bulk-in URB submission and synchronously retire callbacks.
  * Wake blocked readers on USB errors and disconnect, using a persistent
    wait-queue condition instead of a reinitialized completion.
  * Fail probe when the initial bulk reader cannot start.

 -- SMART Board Linux Recovery Project <smartboard-linux@example.org>  Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:20:00 +0200

nw-fermi-sb480 (0.6.5.0-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Register the DKMS source before autoinstalling it.
  * Match the nwfermi character device in usbmisc udev events.
  * Use the documented local daemon path and improve runtime diagnostics.

